      "text": "## Approach\n\nThe Ken French ST_Rev factor is the average of the two low-prior-return (loser) portfolios minus the average of the two high-prior-return (winner) portfolios, using the 2x3 size and prior-return sorts:\n\nST_Rev = 0.5 \u00d7 (Small Lo + Big Lo) \u2212 0.5 \u00d7 (Small Hi + Big Hi)\n\nThe script:\n- Locates the first monthly value-weighted block in the file. The file also contains other blocks, which are ignored.\n- Maps columns by their header names (SMALL/BIG crossed with LO/HI), with a positional fallback (columns 0, 2, 3, 5).\n- Treats -99.99 and -999 as missing and skips any month where one of the four inputs is missing.\n- Writes `output.csv` with `date,value`, where value is in percent.\n\nI have not run this against the full file, so the output is unverified beyond the 60-line excerpt shown.\n\n```python\nimport re\nimport math\nimport csv\n\nFN = \"6_Portfolios_ME_Prior_1_0.csv\"\nOUT = \"output.csv\"\nMISSING = {-99.99, -999.0, -999.99}\nDATE_RE = re.compile(r'^\\s*(\\d{6})\\s*,')\n\n\ndef to_num(s):\n    try:\n        v = float(s.strip())\n    except ValueError:\n        return float(\"nan\")\n    if v in MISSING or math.isclose(v, -99.99) or math.isclose(v, -999.0):\n        return float(\"nan\")\n    return v\n\n\ndef main():\n    with open(FN, encoding=\"latin-1\") as f:\n        lines = f.readlines()\n\n    # Start searching at the \"Value Weighted ... Monthly\" block if present\n    start = 0\n    for i, l in enumerate(lines):\n        if \"value weighted\" in l.lower() and \"monthly\" in l.lower():\n            start = i\n            break\n\n    # Find first data row of that block\n    first = None\n    for i in range(start, len(lines)):\n        if DATE_RE.match(lines[i]):\n            first = i\n            break\n    if first is None:\n        raise SystemExit(\"No data rows found\")\n\n    # Header: nearest preceding line containing commas and portfolio names\n    header = None\n    for i in range(first - 1, -1, -1):\n        if \",\" in lines[i] and \"SMALL\" in lines[i].upper():\n            header = [p.strip().upper() for p in lines[i].split(\",\")]\n            break\n\n    # Determine column indices (in value list, 0-based after date)\n    idx_sl, idx_bl, idx_sh, idx_bh = 0, 3, 2, 5\n    if header is not None:\n        names = header[1:]  # drop the date column label\n        found = {}\n        for j, n in enumerate(names):\n            if \"SMALL\" in n and \"LO\" in n:\n                found[\"sl\"] = j\n            elif \"BIG\" in n and \"LO\" in n:\n                found[\"bl\"] = j\n            elif \"SMALL\" in n and \"HI\" in n:\n                found[\"sh\"] = j\n            elif \"BIG\" in n and \"HI\" in n:\n                found[\"bh\"] = j\n        if len(found) == 4:\n            idx_sl, idx_bl, idx_sh, idx_bh = found[\"sl\"], found[\"bl\"], found[\"sh\"], found[\"bh\"]\n\n    # Collect the contiguous run of data rows\n    rows = []\n    for i in range(first, len(lines)):\n        m = DATE_RE.match(lines[i])\n        if not m:\n            break\n        parts = lines[i].rstrip(\"\\r\\n\").split(\",\")\n        date = int(parts[0].strip())\n        vals = [to_num(p) for p in parts[1:]]\n        if max(idx_sl, idx_bl, idx_sh, idx_bh) >= len(vals):\n            continue\n        sl = vals[idx_sl]\n        bl = vals[idx_bl]\n        sh = vals[idx_sh]\n        bh = vals[idx_bh]\n        if any(math.isnan(x) for x in (sl, bl, sh, bh)):\n            continue\n        st_rev = 0.5 * (sl + bl) - 0.5 * (sh + bh)\n        rows.append((date, st_rev))\n\n    # Deduplicate by date (keep first) and sort\n    seen = {}\n    for d, v in rows:\n        if d not in seen:\n            seen[d] = v\n    with open(OUT, \"w\", newline=\"\") as f:\n        w = csv.writer(f)\n        w.writerow([\"date\", \"value\"])\n        for d in sorted(seen):\n            w.writerow([d, repr(float(seen[d]))])\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```",
